PathwayData.put("data/grammar_vocabulary/units/L03U4.json",{"strand":"grammar_vocabulary","level":3,"cefr":"A2a","unit":4,"theme":"Our Amazing World","essential_question":"How are the places on Earth different from each other?","lessons":[{"id":"GV-L03-U4-LS1","title":"Bigger, Hotter, More Beautiful: Comparative Adjectives","objectives":["Students will be able to form comparatives with -er and more.","Students will be able to compare two places or things with than.","I can say \"Riyadh is hotter than Abha\".","I can say \"The forest is more beautiful than the city\"."],"objectives_ar":["سيتمكن الطلاب من تكوين صيغة المقارنة بـ er وmore.","سيتمكن الطلاب من المقارنة بين مكانين أو شيئين باستخدام than.","أستطيع أن أقول Riyadh is hotter than Abha.","أستطيع أن أقول The forest is more beautiful than the city."],"vocabulary":[{"word":"mountain","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈmaʊntən/","definition":"a very high hill","arabic":"جبل","example":"Jabal Sawda is a mountain near Abha.","image_id":"GV-L03-U4-LS1-W01","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L03-U4-LS1-W01"},{"word":"desert","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈdɛzɚt/","definition":"a very dry place with sand and little rain","arabic":"صحراء","example":"The Rub' al Khali is a huge desert.","image_id":"GV-L03-U4-LS1-W02","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L03-U4-LS1-W02"},{"word":"river","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈrɪvɚ/","definition":"a long line of water that flows to the sea","arabic":"نهر","example":"The Nile is a very long river.","image_id":"GV-L03-U4-LS1-W03","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L03-U4-LS1-W03"},{"word":"ocean","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈoʊʃən/","definition":"a very large sea","arabic":"محيط","example":"The Pacific is the biggest ocean.","image_id":"GV-L03-U4-LS1-W04","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L03-U4-LS1-W04"}],"explanation":{"text":"We use comparative adjectives to compare two things: Saudi Arabia is bigger than Malaysia.\nShort adjectives (one syllable) add -er: tall → taller, cold → colder. Long adjectives (two or more syllables, not ending in -y) use more: beautiful → more beautiful, interesting → more interesting.\nUse than after the comparative. Some comparatives are irregular: good → better, bad → worse, far → farther.\nshort adjective + -er + than: high → higher than\nadjective ending in -y → -ier: dry → drier, happy → happier\nlong adjective → more + adjective + than: more famous than\nirregular: good → better • bad → worse • far → farther","examples":["The Nile is longer than the Thames.","A mountain is higher than a hill.","Winter in Tabuk is colder than winter in Jeddah.","Elephants are heavier than camels.","This book is more interesting than that film.","My new bike is better than my old one.","The weather today is worse than yesterday.","The ocean is deeper than a lake."],"common_errors":["✗ Riyadh is more hot than Abha. → ✓ Riyadh is hotter than Abha. (Short adjective → -er.)","✗ The desert is bigger from the forest. → ✓ The desert is bigger than the forest. (Use than, not from.)","✗ This island is beautifuller. → ✓ This island is more beautiful. (Long adjective → more.)","✗ My cake is more good than yours. → ✓ My cake is better than yours. (good → better.)"],"arabic":"نستخدم صيغة المقارنة لنقارن بين شيئين: Saudi Arabia is bigger than Malaysia.\nالصفة القصيرة نضيف لها er: tall → taller، والطويلة نضع قبلها more: more beautiful.\nنستخدم than (من) بعد صيغة المقارنة، وليس from.\nصيغ شاذة: good → better (أفضل) وbad → worse (أسوأ)."},"video":{"script":[{"time":"00:00–00:20","narration":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “Bigger, Hotter, More Beautiful: Comparative Adjectives”. Let’s learn comparative adjectives (-er than / more … than) and good → better, bad → worse together.","on_screen":"GV-L03-U4-LS1 | Bigger, Hotter, More Beautiful: Comparative Adjectives","visual":"Zaki the Falcon flies in over the Leaf Green title card and lands next to the lesson title; soft chime."},{"time":"00:20–00:45","narration":"Listen to the start of “Two Amazing Countries”: Adam is from Malaysia, but now he lives in Saudi Arabia. He often compares the two countries. Look at the green words.","on_screen":"Adam is from Malaysia, but now he lives in Saudi Arabia. He often compares the two countries.","visual":"Image GV-L03-U4-LS1-IMG01 animates gently; target words glow Leaf Green as they are spoken."},{"time":"00:45–01:30","narration":"We use comparative adjectives to compare two things: Saudi Arabia is bigger than Malaysia. Short adjectives (one syllable) add -er: tall → taller, cold → colder. Long adjectives (two or more syllables, not ending in -y) use more: beautiful → more beautiful, interesting → more interesting.","on_screen":"short adjective + -er + than: high → higher than • adjective ending in -y → -ier: dry → drier, happy → happier • long adjective → more + adjective + than: more famous than","visual":"Grammar box builds line by line (form → meaning → use); Zaki points to each line."},{"time":"01:30–02:15","narration":"Here are some examples. The Nile is longer than the Thames. A mountain is higher than a hill. Winter in Tabuk is colder than winter in Jeddah.","on_screen":"The Nile is longer than the Thames. / A mountain is higher than a hill. / Winter in Tabuk is colder than winter in Jeddah.","visual":"Each example appears on a card with a small picture; the target part bounces once and turns green."},{"time":"02:15–02:45","narration":"Be careful! Some learners say: “Riyadh is more hot than Abha.” That’s not right. We say: “Riyadh is hotter than Abha.” Short adjective → -er.","on_screen":"✗ Riyadh is more hot than Abha.   ✓ Riyadh is hotter than Abha.","visual":"A red cross stamps the wrong sentence; it slides away and the correct sentence appears with a green tick."},{"time":"02:45–03:05","narration":"Quick check: How many things do we compare with \"bigger than\"? … Think! … Two. Great job! Now you can say: I can say \"Riyadh is hotter than Abha\".","on_screen":"Quick check ✔  |  I can: I can say \"Riyadh is hotter than Abha\".","visual":"Three-second pause with a countdown ring; Zaki gives a wing \"thumbs up\" and confetti in the programme colours."}],"captions_ar":["مرحبًا، أنا زكي! درس اليوم: comparative adjectives (-er than / more … than) and good → better, bad → worse.","استمع وانتبه إلى الكلمات الملوّنة بالأخضر.","نستخدم صيغة المقارنة لنقارن بين شيئين: Saudi Arabia is bigger than Malaysia.","لاحظ الأمثلة: الجزء الملوّن هو القاعدة.","انتبه! الخطأ: Riyadh is more hot than Abha. — الصحيح: Riyadh is hotter than Abha.","سؤال سريع… فكّر ثم أجب. أحسنت! الآن تستطيع: أستطيع أن أقول Riyadh is hotter than Abha."]},"texts":[{"type":"reading","title":"Two Amazing Countries","body":"Adam is from Malaysia, but now he lives in Saudi Arabia. He often compares the two countries.\nSaudi Arabia is bigger than Malaysia. It has the Rub' al Khali, one of the largest sand deserts in the world.\nMalaysia is wetter and greener than Saudi Arabia. Its rainforests are older than many other forests.\nIn summer, Riyadh is hotter than Kuala Lumpur, but Kuala Lumpur is more humid.\nAdam thinks the mountains of Abha are cooler and more beautiful than the big cities.\n\"Both countries are amazing!\" he says.","word_count":89,"audio_id":"AUD-GV-L03-U4-LS1-T1"}],"activities":[{"id":"GV-L03-U4-LS1-A1","type":"mcq","instructions":"Controlled practice: Choose the correct answer.","items":[{"q":"A mountain is ___ than a hill.","options":["highest","high","higher","more high"],"answer":"higher","explanation":"Short adjective + -er + than.","explanation_ar":"الصفة القصيرة + er."},{"q":"Jeddah is ___ than Abha in summer.","options":["hottest","hotter","more hot","hoter"],"answer":"hotter","explanation":"Short adjective + -er + than.","explanation_ar":"الصفة القصيرة + er."},{"q":"The museum is ___ than the shopping mall.","options":["more interesting","most interesting","interestinger","interesting"],"answer":"more interesting","explanation":"Long adjective → more + adjective + than.","explanation_ar":"الصفة الطويلة ← more."},{"q":"Saudi Arabia is bigger ___ Malaysia.","options":["then","than","of","from"],"answer":"than","explanation":"Use than after a comparative (not from).","explanation_ar":"نستخدم than بعد المقارنة."},{"q":"My score today is ___ than last week.","options":["gooder","best","more good","better"],"answer":"better","explanation":"good → better; bad → worse; far → farther.","explanation_ar":"صيغ شاذة."},{"q":"The desert is ___ than the forest.","options":["dryier","dryer than","drier","more dry"],"answer":"drier","explanation":"Adjective ending in consonant + y → -ier.","explanation_ar":"الصفة المنتهية بـ y ← ier."}]},{"id":"GV-L03-U4-LS1-B1","type":"gap_fill","instructions":"Guided practice: Write the comparative. Word bank: deeper, more famous, worse","items":[{"q":"The Pacific Ocean is ______ (deep) than the Red Sea.","options":[],"answer":"deeper","explanation":"Short adjective + -er + than.","explanation_ar":"الصفة القصيرة + er."},{"q":"Mount Everest is ______ (famous) than Jabal Sawda.","options":[],"answer":"more famous","explanation":"Long adjective → more + adjective + than.","explanation_ar":"الصفة الطويلة ← more."},{"q":"A rainy day is ______ (bad) for a picnic than a sunny day.","options":[],"answer":"worse","explanation":"good → better; bad → worse; far → farther.","explanation_ar":"صيغ شاذة."}]},{"id":"GV-L03-U4-LS1-B2","type":"open","instructions":"Guided practice: Compare. Write one sentence.","items":[{"q":"a car / a bike (fast)  (compare)","options":[],"answer":"A car is faster than a bike.","explanation":"Short adjective + -er + than.","explanation_ar":"الصفة القصيرة + er."},{"q":"an island / a country (small)  (compare)","options":[],"answer":"An island is smaller than a country.","explanation":"Short adjective + -er + than.","explanation_ar":"الصفة القصيرة + er."},{"q":"gold / silver (expensive)  (compare)","options":[],"answer":"Gold is more expensive than silver.","explanation":"Long adjective → more + adjective + than.","explanation_ar":"الصفة الطويلة ← more."}]},{"id":"GV-L03-U4-LS1-C1","type":"open","instructions":"Freer practice: Compare things you know.","items":[{"q":"My city is ___ than ___.","options":[],"answer":"My city is cooler than Riyadh.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses comparative adjectives (-er than / more … than) and good → better, bad → worse correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"My best friend is ___ than me.","options":[],"answer":"My best friend is taller than me.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses comparative adjectives (-er than / more … than) and good → better, bad → worse correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Math is ___ than ___ for me.","options":[],"answer":"Math is easier than science for me.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses comparative adjectives (-er than / more … than) and good → better, bad → worse correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"___ is more exciting than ___.","options":[],"answer":"Football is more exciting than chess.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses comparative adjectives (-er than / more … than) and good → better, bad → worse correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Summer is ___ than winter in my town.","options":[],"answer":"Summer is hotter than winter in my town.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses comparative adjectives (-er than / more … than) and good → better, bad → worse correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."}]},{"id":"GV-L03-U4-LS1-D1","type":"open","instructions":"Production: Compare two places.","items":[{"q":"Choose two places you know. Write 4 comparisons.","options":[],"answer":"Abha is cooler than Jeddah. Jeddah is bigger than Abha. Abha is greener than Jeddah. Jeddah is busier than Abha.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses comparative adjectives (-er than / more … than) and good → better, bad → worse correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Write 2 comparisons with better or worse.","options":[],"answer":"Fresh juice is better than soda. Fast food is worse than home food.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses comparative adjectives (-er than / more … than) and good → better, bad → worse correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Ask your partner \"Which is bigger, ___ or ___?\" Write his answer.","options":[],"answer":"He thinks the ocean is bigger than the desert.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses comparative adjectives (-er than / more … than) and good → better, bad → worse correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."}]}],"game":{"name":"Four Corners Grammar","mechanic":"timed_quiz","rules":["The teacher says a sentence frame with a cue word and four possible answers (A–D).","Students walk to the corner with the correct answer.","One student in each corner explains the choice in one sentence.","Correct corner scores a point; continue with the next cue."],"data":[{"label":"bigger"},{"label":"hotter"},{"label":"colder"},{"label":"higher"},{"label":"longer"},{"label":"more beautiful"},{"label":"drier"},{"label":"better"}]},"exit_quiz":[{"q":"A river is ___ than a stream.","options":["longest","more long","long","longer"],"answer":"longer","explanation":"Short adjective + -er + than.","explanation_ar":"الصفة القصيرة + er."},{"q":"Snow is ___ than rain.","options":["coldest","colder from","colder","more cold"],"answer":"colder","explanation":"Short adjective + -er + than.","explanation_ar":"الصفة القصيرة + er."},{"q":"This waterfall is ___ than that one.","options":["beautifuller","more beautiful","beautifuler","most beautiful"],"answer":"more beautiful","explanation":"Long adjective → more + adjective + than.","explanation_ar":"الصفة الطويلة ← more."},{"q":"","options":["The Nile is more long than the Jordan River.","The Nile is longer than the Jordan River.","The Nile is longest than the Jordan River.","The Nile is longer from the Jordan River."],"answer":"The Nile is longer than the Jordan River.","explanation":"Use than after a comparative (not from).","explanation_ar":"نستخدم than بعد المقارنة."},{"q":"The traffic is ___ today than yesterday.","options":["worse","badder","more bad","worst"],"answer":"worse","explanation":"good → better; bad → worse; far → farther.","explanation_ar":"صيغ شاذة."},{"q":"A puppy is ___ than a big dog.","options":["smallier","more small","smallest","smaller"],"answer":"smaller","explanation":"Short adjective + -er + than.","explanation_ar":"الصفة القصيرة + er."},{"q":"Sand is ___ than mud.","options":["more dry","dryer than","drier","dryest"],"answer":"drier","explanation":"Adjective ending in consonant + y → -ier.","explanation_ar":"الصفة المنتهية بـ y ← ier."},{"q":"","options":["My grandpa's stories are best than TV.","My grandpa's stories are more good than TV.","My grandpa's stories are gooder than TV.","My grandpa's stories are better than TV."],"answer":"My grandpa's stories are better than TV.","explanation":"good → better; bad → worse; far → farther.","explanation_ar":"صيغ شاذة."},{"q":"An ocean is ___ than a lake.","options":["deeper","deepest","more deep","deep"],"answer":"deeper","explanation":"Short adjective + -er + than.","explanation_ar":"الصفة القصيرة + er."},{"q":"Which comparative is correct?","options":["more expensive","expensivest","more expensiver","expensiver"],"answer":"more expensive","explanation":"Long adjective → more + adjective + than.","explanation_ar":"الصفة الطويلة ← more."}],"images":[{"id":"GV-L03-U4-LS1-IMG01","prompt":"Adam holding two postcards side by side – a Saudi desert with dunes and a green Malaysian rainforest with a waterfall. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Landscape 16:9.","alt":"Adam holding two postcards side by side – a Saudi desert with dunes and a green Malaysian rainforest with a waterfall"},{"id":"GV-L03-U4-LS1-IMG02","prompt":"clean background panel for a grammar box about comparative adjectives (-er than / more … than) and good → better, bad → worse, with Zaki the Falcon pointing at a blank board on the right; leave large empty space for text overlay. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"clean background panel for a grammar box about comparative adjectives (-er than / more … than) and good → better, bad → worse, with Zaki the Falcon pointing at a blank board on the right"},{"id":"GV-L03-U4-LS1-W01","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows mountain (a very high hill); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing mountain: a very high hill"},{"id":"GV-L03-U4-LS1-W02","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows desert (a very dry place with sand and little rain); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing desert: a very dry place with sand and little rain"},{"id":"GV-L03-U4-LS1-W03","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows river (a long line of water that flows to the sea); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing river: a long line of water that flows to the sea"},{"id":"GV-L03-U4-LS1-W04","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows ocean (a very large sea); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing ocean: a very large sea"},{"id":"GV-L03-U4-LS1-G01","prompt":"Card-back and board design for the classroom game “Four Corners Grammar”: Zaki the Falcon icon in the centre, Leaf Green border with navy stars. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image. Portrait 2:3.","alt":"Game card design for Four Corners Grammar"}],"audio":[{"id":"AUD-GV-L03-U4-LS1-W01","script":"mountain. mountain. Jabal Sawda is a mountain near Abha.","voice":"en-US, warm female or male teacher voice","speed":"0.9"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L03-U4-LS1-W02","script":"desert. desert. The Rub' al Khali is a huge desert.","voice":"en-US, warm female or male teacher voice","speed":"0.9"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L03-U4-LS1-W03","script":"river. river. The Nile is a very long river.","voice":"en-US, warm female or male teacher voice","speed":"0.9"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L03-U4-LS1-W04","script":"ocean. ocean. The Pacific is the biggest ocean.","voice":"en-US, warm female or male teacher voice","speed":"0.9"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L03-U4-LS1-T1","script":"Adam is from Malaysia, but now he lives in Saudi Arabia. He often compares the two countries. Saudi Arabia is bigger than Malaysia. It has the Rub' al Khali, one of the largest sand deserts in the world. Malaysia is wetter and greener than Saudi Arabia. Its rainforests are older than many other forests. In summer, Riyadh is hotter than Kuala Lumpur, but Kuala Lumpur is more humid. Adam thinks the mountains of Abha are cooler and more beautiful than the big cities. \"Both countries are amazing!\" he says.","voice":"en-US, warm female or male teacher voice","speed":"0.9"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L03-U4-LS1-VID","script":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “Bigger, Hotter, More Beautiful: Comparative Adjectives”. Let’s learn comparative adjectives (-er than / more … than) and good → better, bad → worse together. Listen to the start of “Two Amazing Countries”: Adam is from Malaysia, but now he lives in Saudi Arabia. He often compares the two countries. Look at the green words. We use comparative adjectives to compare two things: Saudi Arabia is bigger than Malaysia. Short adjectives (one syllable) add -er: tall → taller, cold → colder. Long adjectives (two or more syllables, not ending in -y) use more: beautiful → more beautiful, interesting → more interesting. Here are some examples. The Nile is longer than the Thames. A mountain is higher than a hill. Winter in Tabuk is colder than winter in Jeddah. Be careful! Some learners say: “Riyadh is more hot than Abha.” That’s not right. We say: “Riyadh is hotter than Abha.” Short adjective → -er. Quick check: How many things do we compare with \"bigger than\"? … Think! … Two. Great job! Now you can say: I can say \"Riyadh is hotter than Abha\".","voice":"en-US, Zaki the Falcon narrator voice (bright, friendly)","speed":"0.9"}]},{"id":"GV-L03-U4-LS2","title":"Not as Hot as Riyadh: as … as","objectives":["Students will be able to use as…as to show that two things are the same.","Students will be able to use not as…as to show that two things are different.","I can say \"My bag is as heavy as yours\".","I can say \"Taif isn't as hot as Riyadh\"."],"objectives_ar":["سيتمكن الطلاب من استخدام as…as للتعبير عن تساوي شيئين.","سيتمكن الطلاب من استخدام not as…as للتعبير عن اختلافهما.","أستطيع أن أقول My bag is as heavy as yours.","أستطيع أن أقول Taif isn't as hot as Riyadh."],"vocabulary":[{"word":"island","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈaɪlənd/","definition":"land with water all around it","arabic":"جزيرة","example":"Farasan is a beautiful island in the Red Sea.","image_id":"GV-L03-U4-LS2-W01","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L03-U4-LS2-W01"},{"word":"valley","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈvæli/","definition":"low land between hills or mountains","arabic":"وادٍ","example":"Rain water runs through the valley.","image_id":"GV-L03-U4-LS2-W02","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L03-U4-LS2-W02"},{"word":"forest","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈfɔrəst/","definition":"a large area with many trees","arabic":"غابة","example":"Monkeys live in the forest.","image_id":"GV-L03-U4-LS2-W03","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L03-U4-LS2-W03"},{"word":"lake","pos":"noun","ipa":"/leɪk/","definition":"a large area of water with land all around it","arabic":"بحيرة","example":"We went boating on the lake.","image_id":"GV-L03-U4-LS2-W04","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L03-U4-LS2-W04"}],"explanation":{"text":"Use as + adjective + as when two things are the same: Omar is as tall as Yusuf (the same height).\nUse not as + adjective + as when the first thing has less: Taif isn't as hot as Riyadh = Riyadh is hotter than Taif.\nAfter as … as, use the normal adjective (NOT the comparative): as big as (NOT as bigger as).","examples":["My brother is as tall as my father now.","This test was as easy as the last one.","Taif isn't as hot as Riyadh in summer.","A pony isn't as big as a horse.","Lina's drawing is as good as a real painting!","Is the Red Sea as salty as the Dead Sea? – No, it isn't.","The new park isn't as crowded as the old one.","My grandma is as busy as a bee."],"common_errors":["✗ Ali is as taller as Saad. → ✓ Ali is as tall as Saad. (Use the normal adjective after as.)","✗ The lake is not as deep than the sea. → ✓ The lake is not as deep as the sea. (as … as, not as … than.)","✗ My bag is as heavy like yours. → ✓ My bag is as heavy as yours. (as … as.)"],"arabic":"as + الصفة + as تعني «بنفس الدرجة»: Omar is as tall as Yusuf (بطول يوسف).\nnot as + الصفة + as تعني «أقل»: Taif isn't as hot as Riyadh (الطائف أقل حرارة من الرياض).\nنستخدم الصفة العادية بعد as وليس صيغة المقارنة: as tall as وليس as taller as."},"video":{"script":[{"time":"00:00–00:20","narration":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “Not as Hot as Riyadh: as … as”. Let’s learn (not) as + adjective + as; comparing equal and unequal things together.","on_screen":"GV-L03-U4-LS2 | Not as Hot as Riyadh: as … as","visual":"Zaki the Falcon flies in over the Leaf Green title card and lands next to the lesson title; soft chime."},{"time":"00:20–00:45","narration":"Remember these patterns: Lina is as clever as her sister. The lake isn't as deep as the ocean. Is Abha as hot as Jeddah? – No, it isn't.","on_screen":"Lina is as clever as her sister. | The lake isn't as deep as the ocean. | Is Abha as hot as Jeddah? – No, it isn't.","visual":"Pattern strips slide in from the left; the key words are highlighted in Leaf Green."},{"time":"00:45–01:30","narration":"Use as + adjective + as when two things are the same: Omar is as tall as Yusuf (the same height). Use not as + adjective + as when the first thing has less: Taif isn't as hot as Riyadh = Riyadh is hotter than Taif.","on_screen":"(not) as + adjective + as; comparing equal and unequal things","visual":"Grammar box builds line by line (form → meaning → use); Zaki points to each line."},{"time":"01:30–02:15","narration":"Here are some examples. My brother is as tall as my father now. This test was as easy as the last one. Taif isn't as hot as Riyadh in summer.","on_screen":"My brother is as tall as my father now. / This test was as easy as the last one. / Taif isn't as hot as Riyadh in summer.","visual":"Each example appears on a card with a small picture; the target part bounces once and turns green."},{"time":"02:15–02:45","narration":"Be careful! Some learners say: “Ali is as taller as Saad.” That’s not right. We say: “Ali is as tall as Saad.” Use the normal adjective after as.","on_screen":"✗ Ali is as taller as Saad.   ✓ Ali is as tall as Saad.","visual":"A red cross stamps the wrong sentence; it slides away and the correct sentence appears with a green tick."},{"time":"02:45–03:05","narration":"Quick check: \"Omar is as tall as Yusuf.\" Who is taller? … Think! … Neither – they are the same height. Great job! Now you can say: I can say \"My bag is as heavy as yours\".","on_screen":"Quick check ✔  |  I can: I can say \"My bag is as heavy as yours\".","visual":"Three-second pause with a countdown ring; Zaki gives a wing \"thumbs up\" and confetti in the programme colours."}],"captions_ar":["مرحبًا، أنا زكي! درس اليوم: (not) as + adjective + as; comparing equal and unequal things.","استمع وانتبه إلى الكلمات الملوّنة بالأخضر.","as + الصفة + as تعني «بنفس الدرجة»: Omar is as tall as Yusuf (بطول يوسف).","لاحظ الأمثلة: الجزء الملوّن هو القاعدة.","انتبه! الخطأ: Ali is as taller as Saad. — الصحيح: Ali is as tall as Saad.","سؤال سريع… فكّر ثم أجب. أحسنت! الآن تستطيع: أستطيع أن أقول My bag is as heavy as yours."]},"texts":[],"activities":[{"id":"GV-L03-U4-LS2-A1","type":"mcq","instructions":"Controlled practice: Choose the correct answer.","items":[{"q":"Rakan is 12. Bandar is 12. Rakan is ___ Bandar.","options":["as old as","as old than","as older as","older than"],"answer":"as old as","explanation":"Same → as + adjective + as.","explanation_ar":"التساوي ← as … as."},{"q":"A cat isn't as ___ as a lion.","options":["biggest","more big","bigger","big"],"answer":"big","explanation":"Use the normal adjective inside as … as.","explanation_ar":"الصفة العادية داخل as … as."},{"q":"Taif isn't ___ Riyadh in summer.","options":["as hotter as","hot as","as hot than","as hot as"],"answer":"as hot as","explanation":"Less → not as + adjective + as.","explanation_ar":"الأقل ← not as … as."},{"q":"My answer is as good ___ yours.","options":["like","to","as","than"],"answer":"as","explanation":"Same → as + adjective + as.","explanation_ar":"التساوي ← as … as."},{"q":"A hill isn't as high as a mountain. Which is higher?","options":["the hill","we don't know","the mountain","they are the same"],"answer":"the mountain","explanation":"not as … as = the other one is more.","explanation_ar":"not as … as تعني أن الآخر أكثر."},{"q":"The lake ___ as deep as the ocean.","options":["not","isn't","doesn't","aren't"],"answer":"isn't","explanation":"Less → not as + adjective + as.","explanation_ar":"الأقل ← not as … as."}]},{"id":"GV-L03-U4-LS2-B1","type":"open","instructions":"Guided practice: Rewrite with not as … as.","items":[{"q":"A bike is slower than a car.  (not as … as)","options":[],"answer":"A bike isn't as fast as a car.","explanation":"Less → not as + adjective + as.","explanation_ar":"الأقل ← not as … as."},{"q":"The river is shorter than the Nile.  (not as … as)","options":[],"answer":"The river isn't as long as the Nile.","explanation":"Less → not as + adjective + as.","explanation_ar":"الأقل ← not as … as."},{"q":"My room is smaller than my brother's room.  (not as … as)","options":[],"answer":"My room isn't as big as my brother's room.","explanation":"Less → not as + adjective + as.","explanation_ar":"الأقل ← not as … as."}]},{"id":"GV-L03-U4-LS2-B2","type":"gap_fill","instructions":"Guided practice: Write as … as or not as … as. Word bank: as tall as, not as heavy as, as fast as","items":[{"q":"Twins are often ______ each other. (tall)","options":[],"answer":"as tall as","explanation":"Same → as + adjective + as.","explanation_ar":"التساوي ← as … as."},{"q":"A kitten is ______ a dog. (heavy)","options":[],"answer":"not as heavy as","explanation":"Less → not as + adjective + as.","explanation_ar":"الأقل ← not as … as."},{"q":"My new phone is ______ my dad's phone. (fast)","options":[],"answer":"as fast as","explanation":"Same → as + adjective + as.","explanation_ar":"التساوي ← as … as."}]},{"id":"GV-L03-U4-LS2-C1","type":"open","instructions":"Freer practice: Compare honestly.","items":[{"q":"I am as tall as ___.","options":[],"answer":"I am as tall as my cousin Hamad.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses (not) as + adjective + as; comparing equal and unequal things correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"My city isn't as ___ as Riyadh.","options":[],"answer":"My city isn't as big as Riyadh.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses (not) as + adjective + as; comparing equal and unequal things correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Science is as interesting as ___.","options":[],"answer":"Science is as interesting as history.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses (not) as + adjective + as; comparing equal and unequal things correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"My little brother isn't as ___ as me.","options":[],"answer":"My little brother isn't as fast as me.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses (not) as + adjective + as; comparing equal and unequal things correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"My school is as ___ as ___.","options":[],"answer":"My school is as old as my father's school.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses (not) as + adjective + as; comparing equal and unequal things correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."}]},{"id":"GV-L03-U4-LS2-D1","type":"open","instructions":"Production: Animal comparisons.","items":[{"q":"Write 2 sentences about animals with as … as.","options":[],"answer":"A falcon is as fast as a race car. A cheetah is as fast as a car on the highway.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses (not) as + adjective + as; comparing equal and unequal things correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Write 2 sentences about animals with not as … as.","options":[],"answer":"A turtle isn't as fast as a rabbit. A goat isn't as big as a camel.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses (not) as + adjective + as; comparing equal and unequal things correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Write one sentence about you and a friend with as … as.","options":[],"answer":"I am as good at chess as Faisal.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses (not) as + adjective + as; comparing equal and unequal things correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."}]}],"game":{"name":"Grammar Snakes & Ladders","mechanic":"timed_quiz","rules":["Roll and move. If you land on a cue square, make a sentence with the cue and (not) as + adjective + as; comparing equal and unequal things.","Correct at the bottom of a ladder: climb. Incorrect at the head of a snake: slide down.","Teammates are the judges and must explain any correction.","First player to reach square 30 wins."],"data":[{"cue":"Taif / Riyadh / hot / not as"},{"cue":"a river / an ocean / deep / –"},{"cue":"Abha / Jeddah / cool / +"},{"cue":"my bag / your bag / heavy / as"},{"cue":"a camel / a horse / tall / +"},{"cue":"the Red Sea / the Nile / long / not as"},{"cue":"Malaysia / Saudi Arabia / wet / +"},{"cue":"a lake / a sea / big / not as"},{"cue":"today / yesterday / windy / as"}]},"exit_quiz":[{"q":"My bag is ___ your bag. (same weight)","options":["heavier than as","as heavy than","as heavy as","as heavier as"],"answer":"as heavy as","explanation":"Same → as + adjective + as.","explanation_ar":"التساوي ← as … as."},{"q":"A pond isn't ___ a lake.","options":["as bigger as","as big as","big as","as big than"],"answer":"as big as","explanation":"Less → not as + adjective + as.","explanation_ar":"الأقل ← not as … as."},{"q":"","options":["Sara is as clever than her brother.","Sara is clever as as her brother.","Sara is as cleverer as her brother.","Sara is as clever as her brother."],"answer":"Sara is as clever as her brother.","explanation":"Use the normal adjective inside as … as.","explanation_ar":"الصفة العادية داخل as … as."},{"q":"\"The bus isn't as fast as the train.\" Which is faster?","options":["the train","neither","both","the bus"],"answer":"the train","explanation":"not as … as = the other one is more.","explanation_ar":"not as … as تعني أن الآخر أكثر."},{"q":"","options":["Today isn't as windy than yesterday.","Today isn't as windier as yesterday.","Today isn't as windy as yesterday.","Today isn't windy as yesterday as."],"answer":"Today isn't as windy as yesterday.","explanation":"Less → not as + adjective + as.","explanation_ar":"الأقل ← not as … as."},{"q":"Is your cousin as old as you? – Yes, ___.","options":["he is","he does","he's","is he"],"answer":"he is","explanation":"Same → as + adjective + as.","explanation_ar":"التساوي ← as … as."},{"q":"","options":["This road is as wider as the highway.","This road is as wide like the highway.","This road is wide as the highway.","This road is as wide as the highway."],"answer":"This road is as wide as the highway.","explanation":"Same → as + adjective + as.","explanation_ar":"التساوي ← as … as."},{"q":"A snail ___ as fast as a horse.","options":["isn't","don't","aren't","doesn't"],"answer":"isn't","explanation":"Less → not as + adjective + as.","explanation_ar":"الأقل ← not as … as."},{"q":"","options":["The second film wasn't as better as the first.","The second film wasn't so good like the first.","The second film wasn't as good as the first.","The second film wasn't as good than the first."],"answer":"The second film wasn't as good as the first.","explanation":"Use the normal adjective inside as … as.","explanation_ar":"الصفة العادية داخل as … as."},{"q":"Which means \"Faisal is shorter than Saad\"?","options":["Faisal is as tall as Saad.","Faisal isn't as tall as Saad.","Faisal is taller than Saad.","Saad isn't as tall as Faisal."],"answer":"Faisal isn't as tall as Saad.","explanation":"not as … as = the other one is more.","explanation_ar":"not as … as تعني أن الآخر أكثر."}],"images":[{"id":"GV-L03-U4-LS2-IMG01","prompt":"Two twins standing back to back measuring their height with a ruler, while a thermometer poster compares Taif and Riyadh temperatures. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Landscape 16:9.","alt":"Two twins standing back to back measuring their height with a ruler, while a thermometer poster compares Taif and Riyadh temperatures"},{"id":"GV-L03-U4-LS2-IMG02","prompt":"two-panel visual contrasting correct and incorrect use of (not) as + adjective + as; comparing equal and unequal things: a green tick panel and a soft red cross panel with simple objects from the theme “Our Amazing World”; empty space for text overlay. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"two-panel visual contrasting correct and incorrect use of (not) as + adjective + as"},{"id":"GV-L03-U4-LS2-W01","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows island (land with water all around it); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing island: land with water all around it"},{"id":"GV-L03-U4-LS2-W02","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows valley (low land between hills or mountains); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing valley: low land between hills or mountains"},{"id":"GV-L03-U4-LS2-W03","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows forest (a large area with many trees); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing forest: a large area with many trees"},{"id":"GV-L03-U4-LS2-W04","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows lake (a large area of water with land all around it); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing lake: a large area of water with land all around it"},{"id":"GV-L03-U4-LS2-G01","prompt":"Card-back and board design for the classroom game “Grammar Snakes & Ladders”: Zaki the Falcon icon in the centre, Leaf Green border with navy stars. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image. Portrait 2:3.","alt":"Game card design for Grammar Snakes & Ladders"}],"audio":[{"id":"AUD-GV-L03-U4-LS2-W01","script":"island. island. Farasan is a beautiful island in the Red Sea.","voice":"en-US, warm female or male teacher voice","speed":"0.9"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L03-U4-LS2-W02","script":"valley. valley. Rain water runs through the valley.","voice":"en-US, warm female or male teacher voice","speed":"0.9"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L03-U4-LS2-W03","script":"forest. forest. Monkeys live in the forest.","voice":"en-US, warm female or male teacher voice","speed":"0.9"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L03-U4-LS2-W04","script":"lake. lake. We went boating on the lake.","voice":"en-US, warm female or male teacher voice","speed":"0.9"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L03-U4-LS2-VID","script":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “Not as Hot as Riyadh: as … as”. Let’s learn (not) as + adjective + as; comparing equal and unequal things together. Remember these patterns: Lina is as clever as her sister. The lake isn't as deep as the ocean. Is Abha as hot as Jeddah? – No, it isn't. Use as + adjective + as when two things are the same: Omar is as tall as Yusuf (the same height). Use not as + adjective + as when the first thing has less: Taif isn't as hot as Riyadh = Riyadh is hotter than Taif. Here are some examples. My brother is as tall as my father now. This test was as easy as the last one. Taif isn't as hot as Riyadh in summer. Be careful! Some learners say: “Ali is as taller as Saad.” That’s not right. We say: “Ali is as tall as Saad.” Use the normal adjective after as. Quick check: \"Omar is as tall as Yusuf.\" Who is taller? … Think! … Neither – they are the same height. Great job! Now you can say: I can say \"My bag is as heavy as yours\".","voice":"en-US, Zaki the Falcon narrator voice (bright, friendly)","speed":"0.9"}]},{"id":"GV-L03-U4-LS3","title":"Mountains, Valleys and Oceans: Landforms and Opposites","objectives":["Students will be able to name and describe landforms and bodies of water.","Students will be able to use antonyms to describe and compare places.","I can name landforms like valleys, islands and volcanoes.","I can use opposites like deep/shallow and wet/dry."],"objectives_ar":["سيتمكن الطلاب من تسمية التضاريس والمسطحات المائية ووصفها.","سيتمكن الطلاب من استخدام الأضداد لوصف الأماكن ومقارنتها.","أستطيع أن أسمّي التضاريس مثل الوديان والجزر والبراكين.","أستطيع أن أستخدم الأضداد مثل deep/shallow وwet/dry."],"vocabulary":[{"word":"waterfall","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈwɔtɚˌfɔl/","definition":"water that falls from a high place","arabic":"شلال","example":"The waterfall made a loud noise.","image_id":"GV-L03-U4-LS3-W01","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L03-U4-LS3-W01"},{"word":"volcano","pos":"noun","ipa":"/vɑlˈkeɪnoʊ/","definition":"a mountain that can send out hot rock and fire","arabic":"بركان","example":"There are old volcanoes near Madinah.","image_id":"GV-L03-U4-LS3-W02","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L03-U4-LS3-W02"},{"word":"coast","pos":"noun","ipa":"/koʊst/","definition":"the land next to the sea","arabic":"ساحل","example":"Jeddah is on the Red Sea coast.","image_id":"GV-L03-U4-LS3-W03","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L03-U4-LS3-W03"},{"word":"high","pos":"adjective","ipa":"/haɪ/","definition":"far from the ground; tall (for mountains)","arabic":"مرتفع / عالٍ","example":"The plane flew very high.","image_id":"GV-L03-U4-LS3-W04","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L03-U4-LS3-W04"},{"word":"deep","pos":"adjective","ipa":"/dip/","definition":"going a long way down","arabic":"عميق","example":"The ocean is very deep.","image_id":"GV-L03-U4-LS3-W05","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L03-U4-LS3-W05"}],"explanation":{"text":"Landforms are shapes of the land: mountain, hill, valley, desert, island, volcano, coast. Bodies of water: ocean, sea, river, lake, waterfall.\nUse opposites (antonyms) to describe places: high ↔ low, deep ↔ shallow, wet ↔ dry, hot ↔ cold, wide ↔ narrow.\nIn names, landforms often have capital letters: the Red Sea, the Arabian Gulf, Farasan Islands, Jabal Sawda.\nCollocations/phrases: land: mountain • hill • valley • desert • island • volcano • coast • forest | water: ocean • sea • river • lake • waterfall | high ↔ low • deep ↔ shallow • wet ↔ dry • hot ↔ cold • wide ↔ narrow","examples":["The valley is green after the rain.","Farasan is a group of islands in the Red Sea.","The water near the beach is shallow.","The middle of the ocean is very deep.","Harrat Rahat has old volcanoes.","The waterfall in the park is small but pretty.","Deserts are dry, and rainforests are wet.","Dammam is on the Gulf coast."],"common_errors":["✗ The sea near the beach is low. → ✓ The sea near the beach is shallow. (For water, use shallow (not deep).)","✗ The mountain is very tall and deep. → ✓ The mountain is very high. (Mountains are high; water is deep.)","✗ An island is water with land around it. → ✓ A lake is water with land around it. (An island is land with water around it.)"],"arabic":"التضاريس: mountain (جبل) وvalley (وادٍ) وisland (جزيرة) وvolcano (بركان) وcoast (ساحل).\nالمسطحات المائية: ocean (محيط) وriver (نهر) وlake (بحيرة) وwaterfall (شلال).\nالأضداد: deep (عميق) ↔ shallow (ضحل)، wet (رطب) ↔ dry (جاف)، high (مرتفع) ↔ low (منخفض)."},"video":{"script":[{"time":"00:00–00:20","narration":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “Mountains, Valleys and Oceans: Landforms and Opposites”. Let’s learn geography and landform words; antonyms (high ↔ low, deep ↔ shallow, wet ↔ dry) together.","on_screen":"GV-L03-U4-LS3 | Mountains, Valleys and Oceans: Landforms and Opposites","visual":"Zaki the Falcon flies in over the Leaf Green title card and lands next to the lesson title; soft chime."},{"time":"00:20–00:45","narration":"Meet some new words. waterfall: water that falls from a high place. volcano: a mountain that can send out hot rock and fire. coast: the land next to the sea.","on_screen":"waterfall | volcano | coast","visual":"Each word card flips over to show its picture (vocabulary image briefs) and Arabic meaning."},{"time":"00:45–01:30","narration":"Landforms are shapes of the land: mountain, hill, valley, desert, island, volcano, coast. Bodies of water: ocean, sea, river, lake, waterfall. Use opposites (antonyms) to describe places: high ↔ low, deep ↔ shallow, wet ↔ dry, hot ↔ cold, wide ↔ narrow.","on_screen":"geography and landform words; antonyms (high ↔ low, deep ↔ shallow, wet ↔ dry)","visual":"Grammar box builds line by line (form → meaning → use); Zaki points to each line."},{"time":"01:30–02:15","narration":"Here are some examples. The valley is green after the rain. Farasan is a group of islands in the Red Sea. The water near the beach is shallow.","on_screen":"The valley is green after the rain. / Farasan is a group of islands in the Red Sea. / The water near the beach is shallow.","visual":"Each example appears on a card with a small picture; the target part bounces once and turns green."},{"time":"02:15–02:45","narration":"Be careful! Some learners say: “The sea near the beach is low.” That’s not right. We say: “The sea near the beach is shallow.” For water, use shallow (not deep).","on_screen":"✗ The sea near the beach is low.   ✓ The sea near the beach is shallow.","visual":"A red cross stamps the wrong sentence; it slides away and the correct sentence appears with a green tick."},{"time":"02:45–03:05","narration":"Quick check: Is an island land or water? … Think! … Land, with water all around it. Great job! Now you can say: I can name landforms like valleys, islands and volcanoes.","on_screen":"Quick check ✔  |  I can: I can name landforms like valleys, islands and volcanoes.","visual":"Three-second pause with a countdown ring; Zaki gives a wing \"thumbs up\" and confetti in the programme colours."}],"captions_ar":["مرحبًا، أنا زكي! درس اليوم: geography and landform words; antonyms (high ↔ low, deep ↔ shallow, wet ↔ dry).","استمع وانتبه إلى الكلمات الملوّنة بالأخضر.","التضاريس: mountain (جبل) وvalley (وادٍ) وisland (جزيرة) وvolcano (بركان) وcoast (ساحل).","لاحظ الأمثلة: الجزء الملوّن هو القاعدة.","انتبه! الخطأ: The sea near the beach is low. — الصحيح: The sea near the beach is shallow.","سؤال سريع… فكّر ثم أجب. أحسنت! الآن تستطيع: أستطيع أن أسمّي التضاريس مثل الوديان والجزر والبراكين."]},"texts":[],"activities":[{"id":"GV-L03-U4-LS3-A1","type":"mcq","instructions":"Controlled practice: Choose the correct word.","items":[{"q":"Land with water all around it is an ___.","options":["lake","valley","ocean","island"],"answer":"island","explanation":"Choose the landform that matches the description.","explanation_ar":"اختر التضاريس المناسبة."},{"q":"Low land between two mountains is a ___.","options":["waterfall","coast","volcano","valley"],"answer":"valley","explanation":"Choose the landform that matches the description.","explanation_ar":"اختر التضاريس المناسبة."},{"q":"deep ↔ ___","options":["high","narrow","shallow","wet"],"answer":"shallow","explanation":"Choose the opposite word.","explanation_ar":"اختر الضد."},{"q":"wet ↔ ___","options":["deep","dry","cold","low"],"answer":"dry","explanation":"Choose the opposite word.","explanation_ar":"اختر الضد."},{"q":"Water falling from a high place is a ___.","options":["coast","waterfall","lake","river"],"answer":"waterfall","explanation":"Choose the body of water that matches.","explanation_ar":"اختر المسطح المائي المناسب."},{"q":"A mountain that sends out hot rock is a ___.","options":["volcano","forest","coast","valley"],"answer":"volcano","explanation":"Choose the landform that matches the description.","explanation_ar":"اختر التضاريس المناسبة."}]},{"id":"GV-L03-U4-LS3-B1","type":"match","instructions":"Guided practice: Match the word to the meaning.","items":[{"q":"ocean","options":["a place with many trees","water with land all around it","a very large sea","water that flows to the sea","a dry place with sand","land next to the sea"],"answer":"a very large sea","explanation":"ocean → a very large sea. Choose the landform that matches the description.","explanation_ar":"اختر التضاريس المناسبة."},{"q":"lake","options":["a place with many trees","water with land all around it","a very large sea","water that flows to the sea","a dry place with sand","land next to the sea"],"answer":"water with land all around it","explanation":"lake → water with land all around it. Choose the landform that matches the description.","explanation_ar":"اختر التضاريس المناسبة."},{"q":"coast","options":["a place with many trees","water with land all around it","a very large sea","water that flows to the sea","a dry place with sand","land next to the sea"],"answer":"land next to the sea","explanation":"coast → land next to the sea. Choose the landform that matches the description.","explanation_ar":"اختر التضاريس المناسبة."},{"q":"forest","options":["a place with many trees","water with land all around it","a very large sea","water that flows to the sea","a dry place with sand","land next to the sea"],"answer":"a place with many trees","explanation":"forest → a place with many trees. Choose the landform that matches the description.","explanation_ar":"اختر التضاريس المناسبة."},{"q":"river","options":["a place with many trees","water with land all around it","a very large sea","water that flows to the sea","a dry place with sand","land next to the sea"],"answer":"water that flows to the sea","explanation":"river → water that flows to the sea. Choose the landform that matches the description.","explanation_ar":"اختر التضاريس المناسبة."},{"q":"desert","options":["a place with many trees","water with land all around it","a very large sea","water that flows to the sea","a dry place with sand","land next to the sea"],"answer":"a dry place with sand","explanation":"desert → a dry place with sand. Choose the landform that matches the description.","explanation_ar":"اختر التضاريس المناسبة."}]},{"id":"GV-L03-U4-LS3-C1","type":"open","instructions":"Freer practice: Describe places in Saudi Arabia.","items":[{"q":"A high mountain in Saudi Arabia is ___.","options":[],"answer":"A high mountain in Saudi Arabia is Jabal Sawda.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses geography and landform words; antonyms (high ↔ low, deep ↔ shallow, wet ↔ dry) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"A city on the coast is ___.","options":[],"answer":"A city on the coast is Jeddah.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses geography and landform words; antonyms (high ↔ low, deep ↔ shallow, wet ↔ dry) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"The biggest desert in Saudi Arabia is ___.","options":[],"answer":"The biggest desert is the Rub' al Khali.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses geography and landform words; antonyms (high ↔ low, deep ↔ shallow, wet ↔ dry) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"An island I know is ___.","options":[],"answer":"An island I know is Farasan.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses geography and landform words; antonyms (high ↔ low, deep ↔ shallow, wet ↔ dry) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"A place with old volcanoes is ___.","options":[],"answer":"A place with old volcanoes is near Madinah.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses geography and landform words; antonyms (high ↔ low, deep ↔ shallow, wet ↔ dry) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."}]},{"id":"GV-L03-U4-LS3-D1","type":"open","instructions":"Production: Make a \"Landforms of My Country\" map.","items":[{"q":"Draw a simple map. Label 5 landforms or bodies of water.","options":[],"answer":"Red Sea, Arabian Gulf, Rub' al Khali, Asir mountains, Farasan Islands","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses geography and landform words; antonyms (high ↔ low, deep ↔ shallow, wet ↔ dry) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Write 3 sentences with opposites about your map.","options":[],"answer":"The Red Sea is deep in the middle. The water near the coast is shallow. The desert is dry.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses geography and landform words; antonyms (high ↔ low, deep ↔ shallow, wet ↔ dry) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Write one comparison about two landforms.","options":[],"answer":"The Asir mountains are higher than the hills near Riyadh.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses geography and landform words; antonyms (high ↔ low, deep ↔ shallow, wet ↔ dry) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."}]}],"game":{"name":"Word Dominoes","mechanic":"matching","rules":["Deal the dominoes equally in teams of four.","Player 1 places a domino; the next player adds a domino whose word matches the open definition.","If you cannot play, pass.","The first player with no dominoes left wins."],"data":[{"word":"mountain","match":"a very high hill","arabic":"جبل"},{"word":"desert","match":"a very dry place with sand and little rain","arabic":"صحراء"},{"word":"river","match":"a long line of water that flows to the sea","arabic":"نهر"},{"word":"ocean","match":"a very large sea","arabic":"محيط"},{"word":"island","match":"land with water all around it","arabic":"جزيرة"},{"word":"valley","match":"low land between hills or mountains","arabic":"وادٍ"},{"word":"forest","match":"a large area with many trees","arabic":"غابة"},{"word":"lake","match":"a large area of water with land all around it","arabic":"بحيرة"},{"word":"waterfall","match":"water that falls from a high place","arabic":"شلال"},{"word":"volcano","match":"a mountain that can send out hot rock and fire","arabic":"بركان"},{"word":"coast","match":"the land next to the sea","arabic":"ساحل"},{"word":"high","match":"far from the ground; tall (for mountains)","arabic":"مرتفع / عالٍ"},{"word":"deep","match":"going a long way down","arabic":"عميق"}]},"exit_quiz":[{"q":"Water with land all around it is a ___.","options":["coast","valley","island","lake"],"answer":"lake","explanation":"Choose the body of water that matches.","explanation_ar":"اختر المسطح المائي المناسب."},{"q":"Dammam and Jeddah are on the ___.","options":["desert","volcano","valley","coast"],"answer":"coast","explanation":"Choose the landform that matches the description.","explanation_ar":"اختر التضاريس المناسبة."},{"q":"high ↔ ___","options":["low","wide","deep","dry"],"answer":"low","explanation":"Choose the opposite word.","explanation_ar":"اختر الضد."},{"q":"The water is only 30 cm here. It's ___.","options":["dry","shallow","deep","high"],"answer":"shallow","explanation":"mountains are high; water is deep or shallow.","explanation_ar":"الجبال مرتفعة والماء عميق أو ضحل."},{"q":"A place with many tall trees is a ___.","options":["coast","forest","lake","desert"],"answer":"forest","explanation":"Choose the landform that matches the description.","explanation_ar":"اختر التضاريس المناسبة."},{"q":"Which word is a body of water?","options":["volcano","hill","river","valley"],"answer":"river","explanation":"Choose the body of water that matches.","explanation_ar":"اختر المسطح المائي المناسب."},{"q":"hot ↔ ___","options":["shallow","low","cold","dry"],"answer":"cold","explanation":"Choose the opposite word.","explanation_ar":"اختر الضد."},{"q":"Jabal Sawda is very ___.","options":["wet","high","shallow","deep"],"answer":"high","explanation":"mountains are high; water is deep or shallow.","explanation_ar":"الجبال مرتفعة والماء عميق أو ضحل."},{"q":"The biggest body of water is an ___.","options":["ocean","river","lake","waterfall"],"answer":"ocean","explanation":"Choose the body of water that matches.","explanation_ar":"اختر المسطح المائي المناسب."},{"q":"Very little rain falls in the ___.","options":["desert","valley after rain","forest","lake"],"answer":"desert","explanation":"Choose the landform that matches the description.","explanation_ar":"اختر التضاريس المناسبة."}],"images":[{"id":"GV-L03-U4-LS3-IMG01","prompt":"A labeled landscape poster: a mountain with a waterfall flowing into a valley and river, a forest, a desert with dunes, a volcano, a lake, an island off the coast and the deep blue ocean. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Landscape 16:9.","alt":"A labeled landscape poster: a mountain with a waterfall flowing into a valley and river, a forest, a desert with dunes, a volcano, a lake, an island off the coast and the deep blue ocean"},{"id":"GV-L03-U4-LS3-IMG02","prompt":"word-web visual: a central circle with branches to 5 small picture icons of the lesson words; empty labels. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"word-web visual: a central circle with branches to 5 small picture icons of the lesson words"},{"id":"GV-L03-U4-LS3-W01","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows waterfall (water that falls from a high place); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing waterfall: water that falls from a high place"},{"id":"GV-L03-U4-LS3-W02","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows volcano (a mountain that can send out hot rock and fire); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing volcano: a mountain that can send out hot rock and fire"},{"id":"GV-L03-U4-LS3-W03","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows coast (the land next to the sea); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing coast: the land next to the sea"},{"id":"GV-L03-U4-LS3-W04","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows high (far from the ground; tall (for mountains)); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing high: far from the ground; tall (for mountains)"},{"id":"GV-L03-U4-LS3-W05","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows deep (going a long way down); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing deep: going a long way down"},{"id":"GV-L03-U4-LS3-G01","prompt":"Card-back and board design for the classroom game “Word Dominoes”: Zaki the Falcon icon in the centre, Leaf Green border with navy stars. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image. Portrait 2:3.","alt":"Game card design for Word Dominoes"}],"audio":[{"id":"AUD-GV-L03-U4-LS3-W01","script":"waterfall. waterfall. The waterfall made a loud noise.","voice":"en-US, warm female or male teacher voice","speed":"0.9"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L03-U4-LS3-W02","script":"volcano. volcano. There are old volcanoes near Madinah.","voice":"en-US, warm female or male teacher voice","speed":"0.9"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L03-U4-LS3-W03","script":"coast. coast. Jeddah is on the Red Sea coast.","voice":"en-US, warm female or male teacher voice","speed":"0.9"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L03-U4-LS3-W04","script":"high. high. The plane flew very high.","voice":"en-US, warm female or male teacher voice","speed":"0.9"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L03-U4-LS3-W05","script":"deep. deep. The ocean is very deep.","voice":"en-US, warm female or male teacher voice","speed":"0.9"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L03-U4-LS3-VID","script":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “Mountains, Valleys and Oceans: Landforms and Opposites”. Let’s learn geography and landform words; antonyms (high ↔ low, deep ↔ shallow, wet ↔ dry) together. Meet some new words. waterfall: water that falls from a high place. volcano: a mountain that can send out hot rock and fire. coast: the land next to the sea. Landforms are shapes of the land: mountain, hill, valley, desert, island, volcano, coast. Bodies of water: ocean, sea, river, lake, waterfall. Use opposites (antonyms) to describe places: high ↔ low, deep ↔ shallow, wet ↔ dry, hot ↔ cold, wide ↔ narrow. Here are some examples. The valley is green after the rain. Farasan is a group of islands in the Red Sea. The water near the beach is shallow. Be careful! Some learners say: “The sea near the beach is low.” That’s not right. We say: “The sea near the beach is shallow.” For water, use shallow (not deep). Quick check: Is an island land or water? … Think! … Land, with water all around it. Great job! Now you can say: I can name landforms like valleys, islands and volcanoes.","voice":"en-US, Zaki the Falcon narrator voice (bright, friendly)","speed":"0.9"}]},{"id":"GV-L03-U4-LS4","title":"Bigger, Drier, Better: Spelling Comparatives","objectives":["Students will be able to spell comparatives correctly with -er, -r, -ier and double letters.","Students will be able to choose between -er and more and use irregular forms.","I can spell \"bigger\", \"drier\" and \"larger\".","I can choose between \"-er\" and \"more\"."],"objectives_ar":["سيتمكن الطلاب من تهجئة صيغ المقارنة بشكل صحيح.","سيتمكن الطلاب من الاختيار بين er وmore واستخدام الصيغ الشاذة.","أستطيع أن أتهجّى bigger وdrier وlarger.","أستطيع أن أختار بين er وmore."],"vocabulary":[{"word":"mountain","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈmaʊntən/","definition":"a very high hill","arabic":"جبل","example":"Jabal Sawda is a mountain near Abha.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"desert","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈdɛzɚt/","definition":"a very dry place with sand and little rain","arabic":"صحراء","example":"The Rub' al Khali is a huge desert.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"river","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈrɪvɚ/","definition":"a long line of water that flows to the sea","arabic":"نهر","example":"The Nile is a very long river.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"ocean","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈoʊʃən/","definition":"a very large sea","arabic":"محيط","example":"The Pacific is the biggest ocean.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"island","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈaɪlənd/","definition":"land with water all around it","arabic":"جزيرة","example":"Farasan is a beautiful island in the Red Sea.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"valley","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈvæli/","definition":"low land between hills or mountains","arabic":"وادٍ","example":"Rain water runs through the valley.","image_id":"","audio_id":""}],"explanation":{"text":"Most short adjectives add -er: deep → deeper. Adjectives ending in e add only -r: large → larger, wide → wider.\nOne vowel + one consonant → double the consonant: big → bigger, hot → hotter, wet → wetter. Consonant + y → ier: dry → drier, busy → busier, heavy → heavier.\nLong adjectives use more (no -er): more famous, more dangerous. Irregular: good → better, bad → worse, far → farther.\n+ er: cold → colder, high → higher\ne → + r: safe → safer, nice → nicer\ndouble + er: thin → thinner, sad → sadder\ny → ier: easy → easier, funny → funnier • long → more: more exciting","examples":["The Rub' al Khali is drier than Taif.","My new room is larger than my old one.","July is hotter than March.","The second question was easier.","Abha is wetter than Riyadh.","The road is wider now.","My grandpa's car is older than my dad's.","Today's weather is worse than yesterday's."],"common_errors":["✗ biger → ✓ bigger (Double the g.)","✗ dryer (adjective) → ✓ drier (consonant + y → ier.)","✗ largeer → ✓ larger (Ends in e → add only r.)","✗ more easy → ✓ easier (Two-syllable adjectives ending in y → -ier.)"],"arabic":"معظم الصفات القصيرة نضيف لها er: deeper.\nالمنتهية بـ e نضيف لها r فقط: larger.\nمتحرك واحد + ساكن واحد نضاعف آخره: bigger وhotter. وساكن + y يصبح ier: drier وeasier.\nالصفات الطويلة نستخدم معها more، والشاذة: better وworse."},"video":{"script":[{"time":"00:00–00:20","narration":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “Bigger, Drier, Better: Spelling Comparatives”. Let’s learn spelling comparatives (-er, -r, double consonant + -er, -ier, more, irregular) together.","on_screen":"GV-L03-U4-LS4 | Bigger, Drier, Better: Spelling Comparatives","visual":"Zaki the Falcon flies in over the Leaf Green title card and lands next to the lesson title; soft chime."},{"time":"00:20–00:45","narration":"Most short adjectives add -er: deep → deeper. Adjectives ending in e add only -r: large → larger, wide → wider.","on_screen":"spelling comparatives (-er, -r, double consonant + -er, -ier, more, irregular)","visual":"Pattern strips slide in from the left; the key words are highlighted in Leaf Green."},{"time":"00:45–01:30","narration":"Most short adjectives add -er: deep → deeper. Adjectives ending in e add only -r: large → larger, wide → wider. One vowel + one consonant → double the consonant: big → bigger, hot → hotter, wet → wetter. Consonant + y → ier: dry → drier, busy → busier, heavy → heavier.","on_screen":"+ er: cold → colder, high → higher • e → + r: safe → safer, nice → nicer • double + er: thin → thinner, sad → sadder","visual":"Grammar box builds line by line (form → meaning → use); Zaki points to each line."},{"time":"01:30–02:15","narration":"Here are some examples. The Rub' al Khali is drier than Taif. My new room is larger than my old one. July is hotter than March.","on_screen":"The Rub' al Khali is drier than Taif. / My new room is larger than my old one. / July is hotter than March.","visual":"Each example appears on a card with a small picture; the target part bounces once and turns green."},{"time":"02:15–02:45","narration":"Be careful! Some learners say: “biger.” That’s not right. We say: “bigger.” Double the g.","on_screen":"✗ biger   ✓ bigger","visual":"A red cross stamps the wrong sentence; it slides away and the correct sentence appears with a green tick."},{"time":"02:45–03:05","narration":"Quick check: Why do we double the g in \"bigger\"? … Think! … big = one vowel + one consonant. Great job! Now you can say: I can spell \"bigger\", \"drier\" and \"larger\".","on_screen":"Quick check ✔  |  I can: I can spell \"bigger\", \"drier\" and \"larger\".","visual":"Three-second pause with a countdown ring; Zaki gives a wing \"thumbs up\" and confetti in the programme colours."}],"captions_ar":["مرحبًا، أنا زكي! درس اليوم: spelling comparatives (-er, -r, double consonant + -er, -ier, more, irregular).","استمع وانتبه إلى الكلمات الملوّنة بالأخضر.","معظم الصفات القصيرة نضيف لها er: deeper.","لاحظ الأمثلة: الجزء الملوّن هو القاعدة.","انتبه! الخطأ: biger — الصحيح: bigger","سؤال سريع… فكّر ثم أجب. أحسنت! الآن تستطيع: أستطيع أن أتهجّى bigger وdrier وlarger."]},"texts":[{"type":"reading","title":"Saudi Arabia and Egypt (editing passage)","body":"Saudi Arabia is biger than Egypt. Egypt has the Nile, so some parts of Egypt are greenner than our deserts. The Rub' al Khali is dryer than the Nile valley. In summer, Riyadh is hoter than Cairo. Both countries have more old history than many countries.","word_count":46,"audio_id":""}],"activities":[{"id":"GV-L03-U4-LS4-A1","type":"mcq","instructions":"Controlled practice: Choose the correct spelling.","items":[{"q":"big → ___","options":["bigger","biger","biggeer","more big"],"answer":"bigger","explanation":"One vowel + one consonant → double + er.","explanation_ar":"نضاعف الحرف الأخير."},{"q":"dry → ___","options":["more dry","dryier","dryer than","drier"],"answer":"drier","explanation":"Consonant + y → ier.","explanation_ar":"ساكن + y ← ier."},{"q":"wide → ___","options":["wideer","widder","more wide","wider"],"answer":"wider","explanation":"Ends in e → + r.","explanation_ar":"تنتهي بـ e ← r."},{"q":"cold → ___","options":["colder","coldder","more cold","coldier"],"answer":"colder","explanation":"Most short adjectives: + er.","explanation_ar":"معظم الصفات القصيرة: er."},{"q":"dangerous → ___","options":["dangerousier","more dangerous","dangerouseer","dangerouser"],"answer":"more dangerous","explanation":"Long adjective → more.","explanation_ar":"الصفة الطويلة ← more."},{"q":"bad → ___","options":["badder","worser","worse","more bad"],"answer":"worse","explanation":"Irregular: better, worse, farther.","explanation_ar":"صيغ شاذة."}]},{"id":"GV-L03-U4-LS4-B1","type":"open","instructions":"Guided practice: Correct the spelling mistake.","items":[{"q":"Riyadh is hoter than Abha.","options":[],"answer":"Riyadh is hotter than Abha.","explanation":"hoter → hotter. One vowel + one consonant → double + er.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: hoter → hotter. نضاعف الحرف الأخير."},{"q":"This box is heavyer than that one.","options":[],"answer":"This box is heavier than that one.","explanation":"heavyer → heavier. Consonant + y → ier.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: heavyer → heavier. ساكن + y ← ier."},{"q":"The new stadium is largeer than the old one.","options":[],"answer":"The new stadium is larger than the old one.","explanation":"largeer → larger. Ends in e → + r.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: largeer → larger. تنتهي بـ e ← r."},{"q":"The second test was more easy.","options":[],"answer":"The second test was easier.","explanation":"more easy → easier. Consonant + y → ier.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: more easy → easier. ساكن + y ← ier."},{"q":"Our team is gooder this year.","options":[],"answer":"Our team is better this year.","explanation":"gooder → better. Irregular: better, worse, farther.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: gooder → better. صيغ شاذة."},{"q":"Rainforests are weter than deserts.","options":[],"answer":"Rainforests are wetter than deserts.","explanation":"weter → wetter. One vowel + one consonant → double + er.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: weter → wetter. نضاعف الحرف الأخير."}]},{"id":"GV-L03-U4-LS4-C1","type":"open","instructions":"Freer practice: Edit the geography report.","items":[{"q":"Saudi Arabia is biger than Egypt.","options":[],"answer":"Saudi Arabia is bigger than Egypt.","explanation":"biger → bigger. Most short adjectives: + er.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: biger → bigger. معظم الصفات القصيرة: er."},{"q":"Egypt has the Nile, so some parts of Egypt are greenner than our deserts.","options":[],"answer":"Egypt has the Nile, so some parts of Egypt are greener than our deserts.","explanation":"greenner → greener. Most short adjectives: + er.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: greenner → greener. معظم الصفات القصيرة: er."},{"q":"The Rub' al Khali is dryer than the Nile valley.","options":[],"answer":"The Rub' al Khali is drier than the Nile valley.","explanation":"dryer → drier. Most short adjectives: + er.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: dryer → drier. معظم الصفات القصيرة: er."},{"q":"In summer, Riyadh is hoter than Cairo.","options":[],"answer":"In summer, Riyadh is hotter than Cairo.","explanation":"hoter → hotter. Most short adjectives: + er.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: hoter → hotter. معظم الصفات القصيرة: er."},{"q":"Both countries have more old history than many countries.","options":[],"answer":"Both countries have older history than many countries.","explanation":"more old → older. Most short adjectives: + er.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: more old → older. معظم الصفات القصيرة: er."}]},{"id":"GV-L03-U4-LS4-D1","type":"open","instructions":"Production: Write comparisons.","items":[{"q":"Write 4 comparatives, one for each spelling rule.","options":[],"answer":"taller, safer, thinner, funnier","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses spelling comparatives (-er, -r, double consonant + -er, -ier, more, irregular) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Write 2 sentences comparing two seasons.","options":[],"answer":"Winter is wetter than summer. Summer is hotter than winter.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses spelling comparatives (-er, -r, double consonant + -er, -ier, more, irregular) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Check a partner's comparatives. Write one correction.","options":[],"answer":"\"biger\" → \"bigger\"","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses spelling comparatives (-er, -r, double consonant + -er, -ier, more, irregular) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."}]}],"game":{"name":"Speed Spell","mechanic":"timed_quiz","rules":["The teacher says a word and a short sentence with it.","Students write the word in 10 seconds.","Show boards on \"Show me!\". Correct = 1 point.","After 10 words, partners check each other's boards and correct any mistakes."],"data":[{"word":"bigger","clue":""},{"word":"hotter","clue":""},{"word":"wetter","clue":""},{"word":"drier","clue":""},{"word":"easier","clue":""},{"word":"larger","clue":""},{"word":"wider","clue":""},{"word":"higher","clue":""},{"word":"better","clue":""},{"word":"worse","clue":""},{"word":"mountain","clue":"a very high hill"},{"word":"desert","clue":"a very dry place with sand and little rain"}]},"exit_quiz":[{"q":"hot → ___","options":["more hot","hotter","hoter","hotteer"],"answer":"hotter","explanation":"One vowel + one consonant → double + er.","explanation_ar":"نضاعف الحرف الأخير."},{"q":"busy → ___","options":["more busy","busier","busyer","busyier"],"answer":"busier","explanation":"Consonant + y → ier.","explanation_ar":"ساكن + y ← ier."},{"q":"nice → ___","options":["nicier","niceer","nicer","more nice"],"answer":"nicer","explanation":"Ends in e → + r.","explanation_ar":"تنتهي بـ e ← r."},{"q":"","options":["The new mall is biger than the old one.","The new mall is more big than the old one.","The new mall is biggeer than the old one.","The new mall is bigger than the old one."],"answer":"The new mall is bigger than the old one.","explanation":"One vowel + one consonant → double + er.","explanation_ar":"نضاعف الحرف الأخير."},{"q":"famous → ___","options":["more famous","famouseer","famousier","famouser"],"answer":"more famous","explanation":"Long adjective → more.","explanation_ar":"الصفة الطويلة ← more."},{"q":"","options":["This puzzle is easier than that one.","This puzzle is easyier than that one.","This puzzle is easyer than that one.","This puzzle is more easy than that one."],"answer":"This puzzle is easier than that one.","explanation":"Consonant + y → ier.","explanation_ar":"ساكن + y ← ier."},{"q":"good → ___","options":["more good","best","better","gooder"],"answer":"better","explanation":"Irregular: better, worse, farther.","explanation_ar":"صيغ شاذة."},{"q":"","options":["The river is wider here.","The river is widder here.","The river is more wide here.","The river is wideer here."],"answer":"The river is wider here.","explanation":"Ends in e → + r.","explanation_ar":"تنتهي بـ e ← r."},{"q":"thin → ___","options":["thinier","thiner","more thin","thinner"],"answer":"thinner","explanation":"One vowel + one consonant → double + er.","explanation_ar":"نضاعف الحرف الأخير."},{"q":"Which comparative is spelled correctly?","options":["sadeer","saddier","sadder","sader"],"answer":"sadder","explanation":"One vowel + one consonant → double + er.","explanation_ar":"نضاعف الحرف الأخير."}],"images":[{"id":"GV-L03-U4-LS4-IMG01","prompt":"Two or three of the programme characters in a scene about “Our Amazing World” that shows spelling comparatives (-er, -r, double consonant + -er, -ier, more, irregular) in action. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Landscape 16:9.","alt":"Two or three of the programme characters in a scene about “Our Amazing World” that shows spelling comparatives (-er, -r, double consonant + -er, -ier, more, irregular) in action"},{"id":"GV-L03-U4-LS4-IMG02","prompt":"friendly editing-desk scene: a magnifying glass over a page with highlighted punctuation marks, Zaki holding a green pen. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"friendly editing-desk scene: a magnifying glass over a page with highlighted punctuation marks, Zaki holding a green pen"},{"id":"GV-L03-U4-LS4-G01","prompt":"Card-back and board design for the classroom game “Speed Spell”: Zaki the Falcon icon in the centre, Leaf Green border with navy stars. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image. Portrait 2:3.","alt":"Game card design for Speed Spell"}],"audio":[{"id":"AUD-GV-L03-U4-LS4-VID","script":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “Bigger, Drier, Better: Spelling Comparatives”. Let’s learn spelling comparatives (-er, -r, double consonant + -er, -ier, more, irregular) together. Most short adjectives add -er: deep → deeper. Adjectives ending in e add only -r: large → larger, wide → wider. Most short adjectives add -er: deep → deeper. Adjectives ending in e add only -r: large → larger, wide → wider. One vowel + one consonant → double the consonant: big → bigger, hot → hotter, wet → wetter. Consonant + y → ier: dry → drier, busy → busier, heavy → heavier. Here are some examples. The Rub' al Khali is drier than Taif. My new room is larger than my old one. July is hotter than March. Be careful! Some learners say: “biger.” That’s not right. We say: “bigger.” Double the g. Quick check: Why do we double the g in \"bigger\"? … Think! … big = one vowel + one consonant. Great job! Now you can say: I can spell \"bigger\", \"drier\" and \"larger\".","voice":"en-US, Zaki the Falcon narrator voice (bright, friendly)","speed":"0.9"}]},{"id":"GV-L03-U4-LS5","title":"Compare Two Places: Language in Use","objectives":["Students will be able to compare two places in a discussion.","Students will be able to write a comparison paragraph using comparatives and as…as.","I can compare two places with a partner.","I can write a paragraph comparing two places."],"objectives_ar":["سيتمكن الطلاب من المقارنة بين مكانين في نقاش.","سيتمكن الطلاب من كتابة فقرة مقارنة باستخدام صيغ المقارنة وas…as.","أستطيع أن أقارن بين مكانين مع زميلي.","أستطيع أن أكتب فقرة تقارن بين مكانين."],"vocabulary":[{"word":"mountain","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈmaʊntən/","definition":"a very high hill","arabic":"جبل","example":"Jabal Sawda is a mountain near Abha.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"desert","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈdɛzɚt/","definition":"a very dry place with sand and little rain","arabic":"صحراء","example":"The Rub' al Khali is a huge desert.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"river","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈrɪvɚ/","definition":"a long line of water that flows to the sea","arabic":"نهر","example":"The Nile is a very long river.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"ocean","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈoʊʃən/","definition":"a very large sea","arabic":"محيط","example":"The Pacific is the biggest ocean.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"island","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈaɪlənd/","definition":"land with water all around it","arabic":"جزيرة","example":"Farasan is a beautiful island in the Red Sea.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"valley","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈvæli/","definition":"low land between hills or mountains","arabic":"وادٍ","example":"Rain water runs through the valley.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"forest","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈfɔrəst/","definition":"a large area with many trees","arabic":"غابة","example":"Monkeys live in the forest.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"lake","pos":"noun","ipa":"/leɪk/","definition":"a large area of water with land all around it","arabic":"بحيرة","example":"We went boating on the lake.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"waterfall","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈwɔtɚˌfɔl/","definition":"water that falls from a high place","arabic":"شلال","example":"The waterfall made a loud noise.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"volcano","pos":"noun","ipa":"/vɑlˈkeɪnoʊ/","definition":"a mountain that can send out hot rock and fire","arabic":"بركان","example":"There are old volcanoes near Madinah.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"coast","pos":"noun","ipa":"/koʊst/","definition":"the land next to the sea","arabic":"ساحل","example":"Jeddah is on the Red Sea coast.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"high","pos":"adjective","ipa":"/haɪ/","definition":"far from the ground; tall (for mountains)","arabic":"مرتفع / عالٍ","example":"The plane flew very high.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"deep","pos":"adjective","ipa":"/dip/","definition":"going a long way down","arabic":"عميق","example":"The ocean is very deep.","image_id":"","audio_id":""}],"explanation":{"text":"Today you use all of Unit 4: comparatives (-er/more … than), as … as, not as … as, landform words and comparative spelling.\nA comparison paragraph says how two places are the same and how they are different. Use linking words: both, but, so.\n✔ -er than / more … than / better / worse\n✔ as … as (same) and not as … as (less)\n✔ landform words: mountain, coast, valley, desert\n✔ correct spelling: bigger, drier, larger","examples":["Abha is cooler than Jeddah.","Jeddah is busier than Abha.","The mountains are higher than the hills.","The beach isn't as quiet as the valley.","Both cities are as friendly as each other.","The sea is deeper than the lake.","Riyadh is drier than Abha.","For me, the mountains are more exciting than the city."],"common_errors":["✗ Abha is more cool than Jeddah. → ✓ Abha is cooler than Jeddah. (Short adjective → -er.)","✗ Jeddah is busyer than Abha. → ✓ Jeddah is busier than Abha. (y → ier.)","✗ Abha isn't as warmer as Jeddah. → ✓ Abha isn't as warm as Jeddah. (Normal adjective in as … as.)"],"arabic":"نراجع صيغ المقارنة وas…as وكلمات التضاريس وتهجئة المقارنة.\nفقرة المقارنة توضح أوجه الشبه والاختلاف، ونستخدم both وbut وso للربط.\nتذكّر: الصفة القصيرة + er، والطويلة مع more، والعادية داخل as…as."},"video":{"script":[{"time":"00:00–00:20","narration":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “Compare Two Places: Language in Use”. Let’s learn comparatives, as…as, landform words and comparative spelling (unit review) together.","on_screen":"GV-L03-U4-LS5 | Compare Two Places: Language in Use","visual":"Zaki the Falcon flies in over the Leaf Green title card and lands next to the lesson title; soft chime."},{"time":"00:20–00:45","narration":"Let’s use everything from this unit. Your task: Travel debate: in pairs, one student chooses the mountains (Abha) and one chooses the coast (Jeddah). Each gives 3 reasons with comparatives and as…as. The class votes for the best holiday place.","on_screen":"Language in use","visual":"Split screen: two cast members talking, with speech bubbles appearing."},{"time":"00:45–01:30","narration":"Today you use all of Unit 4: comparatives (-er/more … than), as … as, not as … as, landform words and comparative spelling. A comparison paragraph says how two places are the same and how they are different. Use linking words: both, but, so.","on_screen":"✔ -er than / more … than / better / worse • ✔ as … as (same) and not as … as (less) • ✔ landform words: mountain, coast, valley, desert","visual":"Grammar box builds line by line (form → meaning → use); Zaki points to each line."},{"time":"01:30–02:15","narration":"Here are some examples. Abha is cooler than Jeddah. Jeddah is busier than Abha. The mountains are higher than the hills.","on_screen":"Abha is cooler than Jeddah. / Jeddah is busier than Abha. / The mountains are higher than the hills.","visual":"Each example appears on a card with a small picture; the target part bounces once and turns green."},{"time":"02:15–02:45","narration":"Be careful! Some learners say: “Abha is more cool than Jeddah.” That’s not right. We say: “Abha is cooler than Jeddah.” Short adjective → -er.","on_screen":"✗ Abha is more cool than Jeddah.   ✓ Abha is cooler than Jeddah.","visual":"A red cross stamps the wrong sentence; it slides away and the correct sentence appears with a green tick."},{"time":"02:45–03:05","narration":"Quick check: what is wrong with “Jeddah is busyer than Abha.”? … Think! … It should be “Jeddah is busier than Abha.”. Great job! Now you can say: I can compare two places with a partner.","on_screen":"Quick check ✔  |  I can: I can compare two places with a partner.","visual":"Three-second pause with a countdown ring; Zaki gives a wing \"thumbs up\" and confetti in the programme colours."}],"captions_ar":["مرحبًا، أنا زكي! درس اليوم: comparatives, as…as, landform words and comparative spelling (unit review).","استمع وانتبه إلى الكلمات الملوّنة بالأخضر.","نراجع صيغ المقارنة وas…as وكلمات التضاريس وتهجئة المقارنة.","لاحظ الأمثلة: الجزء الملوّن هو القاعدة.","انتبه! الخطأ: Abha is more cool than Jeddah. — الصحيح: Abha is cooler than Jeddah.","سؤال سريع… فكّر ثم أجب. أحسنت! الآن تستطيع: أستطيع أن أقارن بين مكانين مع زميلي."]},"texts":[{"type":"model","title":"Abha or Jeddah? – Sara","body":"Abha and Jeddah are both beautiful cities, but they are very different.\nAbha is in the mountains, so it is higher and cooler than Jeddah.\nJeddah is on the coast. It is bigger and busier than Abha, and the sea is warmer than the mountain lakes.\nIn summer, Jeddah isn't as cool as Abha, but its beaches are amazing.\nAbha's markets are as interesting as Jeddah's old Balad.\nFor me, Abha is better for a summer holiday!","word_count":77,"audio_id":"AUD-GV-L03-U4-LS5-T1"}],"activities":[{"id":"GV-L03-U4-LS5-A1","type":"true_false","instructions":"Controlled practice: Read Sara's paragraph. True or False?","items":[{"q":"Abha is higher and cooler than Jeddah.","options":["True","False"],"answer":"True","explanation":"Check the text “Abha or Jeddah? – Sara”.","explanation_ar":"ارجع إلى النص وابحث عن الجملة التي تعطي الإجابة."},{"q":"Jeddah is in the mountains.","options":["True","False"],"answer":"False","explanation":"Check the text “Abha or Jeddah? – Sara”.","explanation_ar":"ارجع إلى النص وابحث عن الجملة التي تعطي الإجابة."},{"q":"Jeddah is bigger and busier than Abha.","options":["True","False"],"answer":"True","explanation":"Check the text “Abha or Jeddah? – Sara”.","explanation_ar":"ارجع إلى النص وابحث عن الجملة التي تعطي الإجابة."},{"q":"In summer, Jeddah is as cool as Abha.","options":["True","False"],"answer":"False","explanation":"Check the text “Abha or Jeddah? – Sara”.","explanation_ar":"ارجع إلى النص وابحث عن الجملة التي تعطي الإجابة."},{"q":"Sara thinks Abha's markets are as interesting as Jeddah's Balad.","options":["True","False"],"answer":"True","explanation":"Check the text “Abha or Jeddah? – Sara”.","explanation_ar":"ارجع إلى النص وابحث عن الجملة التي تعطي الإجابة."},{"q":"Sara prefers Jeddah for a summer holiday.","options":["True","False"],"answer":"False","explanation":"Check the text “Abha or Jeddah? – Sara”.","explanation_ar":"ارجع إلى النص وابحث عن الجملة التي تعطي الإجابة."}]},{"id":"GV-L03-U4-LS5-B1","type":"mcq","instructions":"Guided practice: Choose the correct answer.","items":[{"q":"Abha is ___ than Jeddah.","options":["more high","higher","highest","high"],"answer":"higher","explanation":"Comparative: -er/more + than.","explanation_ar":"صيغة المقارنة."},{"q":"Jeddah isn't ___ Abha in summer.","options":["as cool as","as cool than","as cooler as","cool as"],"answer":"as cool as","explanation":"as + adjective + as / not as … as.","explanation_ar":"as…as."},{"q":"Jeddah is on the ___.","options":["coast","valley","volcano","desert"],"answer":"coast","explanation":"Choose the right landform word.","explanation_ar":"كلمة التضاريس المناسبة."},{"q":"Jeddah is ___ than Abha.","options":["busyier","busyer","more busy","busier"],"answer":"busier","explanation":"Check the comparative spelling.","explanation_ar":"تحقق من التهجئة."},{"q":"Both cities are beautiful, ___ they are different.","options":["because","than","but","so"],"answer":"but","explanation":"Use both / but / so to link ideas.","explanation_ar":"أدوات الربط."},{"q":"The sea is ___ than the mountain lakes.","options":["warmmer","more warm","warmest","warmer"],"answer":"warmer","explanation":"Comparative: -er/more + than.","explanation_ar":"صيغة المقارنة."}]},{"id":"GV-L03-U4-LS5-C1","type":"open","instructions":"Freer practice: Travel debate. Write your reasons.","items":[{"q":"My place is ___ than your place.","options":[],"answer":"The mountains are cooler than the coast.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses comparatives, as…as, landform words and comparative spelling (unit review) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"My place has ___ than your place.","options":[],"answer":"My place has more green valleys.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses comparatives, as…as, landform words and comparative spelling (unit review) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Your place isn't as ___ as mine.","options":[],"answer":"Your place isn't as quiet as mine.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses comparatives, as…as, landform words and comparative spelling (unit review) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"My place is as ___ as yours.","options":[],"answer":"My place is as beautiful as yours.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses comparatives, as…as, landform words and comparative spelling (unit review) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"The class voted for ___.","options":[],"answer":"The class voted for Abha.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses comparatives, as…as, landform words and comparative spelling (unit review) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."}]},{"id":"GV-L03-U4-LS5-D1","type":"open","instructions":"Production: Write your comparison paragraph.","items":[{"q":"Plan: two places, 3 differences, 1 thing that is the same.","options":[],"answer":"Taif and Riyadh; Taif cooler, greener, smaller; both have great food","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses comparatives, as…as, landform words and comparative spelling (unit review) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Write your comparison paragraph in 6–7 sentences.","options":[],"answer":"Taif and Riyadh are both great cities. Taif is cooler and greener than Riyadh. Riyadh is bigger and busier. In summer, Riyadh isn't as pleasant as Taif. The food in Taif is as delicious as the food in Riyadh. I think Taif is better for a holiday.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses comparatives, as…as, landform words and comparative spelling (unit review) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Check: -er/more? as … as? spelling? Fix one mistake.","options":[],"answer":"I changed \"more cool\" to \"cooler\".","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses comparatives, as…as, landform words and comparative spelling (unit review) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."}]}],"game":{"name":"Spin the Review Wheel","mechanic":"spin_wheel","rules":["A player spins the wheel and lands on a word.","Say what the word means and use it in a sentence with comparatives, as…as, landform words and comparative spelling (unit review).","Teammates check: meaning (1 point), grammar (1 point), pronunciation (1 point).","Highest total after 6 minutes wins."],"data":[{"cue":"mountain","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"desert","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"river","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"ocean","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"island","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"valley","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"forest","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"lake","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"waterfall","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"volcano","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"coast","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"high","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"deep","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]}]},"exit_quiz":[{"q":"A volcano is ___ than a hill.","options":["most dangerous","more dangerous","dangerouser","dangerous"],"answer":"more dangerous","explanation":"Comparative: -er/more + than.","explanation_ar":"صيغة المقارنة."},{"q":"","options":["The lake isn't big as the sea.","The lake isn't as big than the sea.","The lake isn't as big as the sea.","The lake isn't as bigger as the sea."],"answer":"The lake isn't as big as the sea.","explanation":"as + adjective + as / not as … as.","explanation_ar":"as…as."},{"q":"Low land between hills is a ___.","options":["volcano","coast","island","valley"],"answer":"valley","explanation":"Choose the right landform word.","explanation_ar":"كلمة التضاريس المناسبة."},{"q":"","options":["The desert is more dry than the coast.","The desert is drier than the coast.","The desert is dryer than the coast.","The desert is dryier than the coast."],"answer":"The desert is drier than the coast.","explanation":"Check the comparative spelling.","explanation_ar":"تحقق من التهجئة."},{"q":"It was very hot, ___ we went to the beach.","options":["but","than","as","so"],"answer":"so","explanation":"Use both / but / so to link ideas.","explanation_ar":"أدوات الربط."},{"q":"My new school is ___ than my old school.","options":["best","more good","better","gooder"],"answer":"better","explanation":"Comparative: -er/more + than.","explanation_ar":"صيغة المقارنة."},{"q":"","options":["My cousin is as tall as me.","My cousin is tall as me.","My cousin is as taller as me.","My cousin is as tall than me."],"answer":"My cousin is as tall as me.","explanation":"as + adjective + as / not as … as.","explanation_ar":"as…as."},{"q":"The Farasan ___ are in the Red Sea.","options":["Islands","Valleys","Deserts","Volcanoes"],"answer":"Islands","explanation":"Choose the right landform word.","explanation_ar":"كلمة التضاريس المناسبة."},{"q":"","options":["Winter in Tabuk is more cold than winter in Jeddah.","Winter in Tabuk is coldder than winter in Jeddah.","Winter in Tabuk is colder than winter in Jeddah.","Winter in Tabuk is colder from winter in Jeddah."],"answer":"Winter in Tabuk is colder than winter in Jeddah.","explanation":"Comparative: -er/more + than.","explanation_ar":"صيغة المقارنة."},{"q":"Pick the best sentence for a comparison paragraph:","options":["Both city is friendly, but Riyadh is biger than Taif.","Both cities are friendly, so Riyadh is bigger from Taif.","Both cities are friendly, but Riyadh is more big than Taif.","Both cities are friendly, but Riyadh is bigger than Taif."],"answer":"Both cities are friendly, but Riyadh is bigger than Taif.","explanation":"Use both / but / so to link ideas.","explanation_ar":"أدوات الربط."}],"images":[{"id":"GV-L03-U4-LS5-IMG01","prompt":"Lina and Sara looking at a globe and two photos – the cool green mountains of Abha and the warm blue coast of Jeddah – with a Venn diagram on paper. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Landscape 16:9.","alt":"Lina and Sara looking at a globe and two photos – the cool green mountains of Abha and the warm blue coast of Jeddah – with a Venn diagram on paper"},{"id":"GV-L03-U4-LS5-IMG02","prompt":"two programme characters doing the speaking task about “Our Amazing World”, speech bubbles left empty. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"two programme characters doing the speaking task about “Our Amazing World”, speech bubbles left empty"},{"id":"GV-L03-U4-LS5-G01","prompt":"Card-back and board design for the classroom game “Spin the Review Wheel”: Zaki the Falcon icon in the centre, Leaf Green border with navy stars. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image. Portrait 2:3.","alt":"Game card design for Spin the Review Wheel"}],"audio":[{"id":"AUD-GV-L03-U4-LS5-T1","script":"Abha and Jeddah are both beautiful cities, but they are very different. Abha is in the mountains, so it is higher and cooler than Jeddah. Jeddah is on the coast. It is bigger and busier than Abha, and the sea is warmer than the mountain lakes. In summer, Jeddah isn't as cool as Abha, but its beaches are amazing. Abha's markets are as interesting as Jeddah's old Balad. For me, Abha is better for a summer holiday!","voice":"en-US, warm female or male teacher voice","speed":"0.9"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L03-U4-LS5-VID","script":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “Compare Two Places: Language in Use”. Let’s learn comparatives, as…as, landform words and comparative spelling (unit review) together. Let’s use everything from this unit. Your task: Travel debate: in pairs, one student chooses the mountains (Abha) and one chooses the coast (Jeddah). Each gives 3 reasons with comparatives and as…as. The class votes for the best holiday place. Today you use all of Unit 4: comparatives (-er/more … than), as … as, not as … as, landform words and comparative spelling. A comparison paragraph says how two places are the same and how they are different. Use linking words: both, but, so. Here are some examples. Abha is cooler than Jeddah. Jeddah is busier than Abha. The mountains are higher than the hills. Be careful! Some learners say: “Abha is more cool than Jeddah.” That’s not right. We say: “Abha is cooler than Jeddah.” Short adjective → -er. Quick check: what is wrong with “Jeddah is busyer than Abha.”? … Think! … It should be “Jeddah is busier than Abha.”. Great job! Now you can say: I can compare two places with a partner.","voice":"en-US, Zaki the Falcon narrator voice (bright, friendly)","speed":"0.9"}]}],"unit_test":[{"q":"An elephant is ___ than a horse.","options":["heavier","heaviest","more heavy","heavyer"],"answer":"heavier","explanation":"Adjective ending in consonant + y → -ier.","explanation_ar":"الصفة المنتهية بـ y ← ier."},{"q":"The Amazon is a ___ river than the Thames.","options":["longest","long","longer","more long"],"answer":"longer","explanation":"Short adjective + -er + than.","explanation_ar":"الصفة القصيرة + er."},{"q":"The new library is ___ than the old one.","options":["moderner","most modern","modern","more modern"],"answer":"more modern","explanation":"Long adjective → more + adjective + than.","explanation_ar":"الصفة الطويلة ← more."},{"q":"Riyadh is bigger ___ Taif.","options":["then","than","from","of"],"answer":"than","explanation":"Use than after a comparative (not from).","explanation_ar":"نستخدم than بعد المقارنة."},{"q":"My little sister's drawing is ___ than mine!","options":["gooder","best","more good","better"],"answer":"better","explanation":"good → better; bad → worse; far → farther.","explanation_ar":"صيغ شاذة."},{"q":"A pony isn't ___ a horse.","options":["as big than","big as","as bigger as","as big as"],"answer":"as big as","explanation":"Less → not as + adjective + as.","explanation_ar":"الأقل ← not as … as."},{"q":"","options":["Hamad is as strong than his brother.","Hamad is strong as as his brother.","Hamad is as strong as his brother.","Hamad is as stronger as his brother."],"answer":"Hamad is as strong as his brother.","explanation":"Use the normal adjective inside as … as.","explanation_ar":"الصفة العادية داخل as … as."},{"q":"\"A cheetah isn't as slow as a turtle.\" Which is slower?","options":["the turtle","neither","both","the cheetah"],"answer":"the turtle","explanation":"not as … as = the other one is more.","explanation_ar":"not as … as تعني أن الآخر أكثر."},{"q":"Is Abha as hot as Riyadh? – No, it ___.","options":["aren't","not","doesn't","isn't"],"answer":"isn't","explanation":"Same → as + adjective + as.","explanation_ar":"التساوي ← as … as."},{"q":"Farasan has the sea on every side. It is an ___.","options":["river","island","ocean","valley"],"answer":"island","explanation":"Choose the landform that matches the description.","explanation_ar":"اختر التضاريس المناسبة."},{"q":"The water near the shore is only knee-deep. It's ___.","options":["shallow","dry","high","deep"],"answer":"shallow","explanation":"mountains are high; water is deep or shallow.","explanation_ar":"الجبال مرتفعة والماء عميق أو ضحل."},{"q":"dry ↔ ___","options":["low","narrow","shallow","wet"],"answer":"wet","explanation":"Choose the opposite word.","explanation_ar":"اختر الضد."},{"q":"Water that falls down rocks is a ___.","options":["coast","lake","waterfall","valley"],"answer":"waterfall","explanation":"Choose the body of water that matches.","explanation_ar":"اختر المسطح المائي المناسب."},{"q":"Which one is a landform?","options":["valley","river","lake","ocean"],"answer":"valley","explanation":"Choose the landform that matches the description.","explanation_ar":"اختر التضاريس المناسبة."},{"q":"Mountains are ___.","options":["deep","high","shallow","wet"],"answer":"high","explanation":"mountains are high; water is deep or shallow.","explanation_ar":"الجبال مرتفعة والماء عميق أو ضحل."},{"q":"The Arabian Gulf is next to the east ___ of Saudi Arabia.","options":["volcano","forest","desert","coast"],"answer":"coast","explanation":"Choose the landform that matches the description.","explanation_ar":"اختر التضاريس المناسبة."},{"q":"wet → ___","options":["wettier","wetter","weter","more wet"],"answer":"wetter","explanation":"One vowel + one consonant → double + er.","explanation_ar":"نضاعف الحرف الأخير."},{"q":"easy → ___","options":["more easy","easier","easyer","easyier"],"answer":"easier","explanation":"Adjective ending in consonant + y → -ier.","explanation_ar":"الصفة المنتهية بـ y ← ier."},{"q":"safe → ___","options":["safer","saffer","more safe","safeer"],"answer":"safer","explanation":"Ends in e → + r.","explanation_ar":"تنتهي بـ e ← r."},{"q":"","options":["This mountain is more high than that one.","This mountain is higheer than that one.","This mountain is higher than that one.","This mountain is highier than that one."],"answer":"This mountain is higher than that one.","explanation":"Short adjective + -er + than.","explanation_ar":"الصفة القصيرة + er."},{"q":"","options":["The traffic in the city is worse than in the village.","The traffic in the city is badder than in the village.","The traffic in the city is worser than in the village.","The traffic in the city is more bad than in the village."],"answer":"The traffic in the city is worse than in the village.","explanation":"good → better; bad → worse; far → farther.","explanation_ar":"صيغ شاذة."},{"q":"Pick the best sentence for a geography report:","options":["The ocean is more deep and largeer than a lake.","The ocean is deeper and larger than a lake.","The ocean is deeper and larger from a lake.","The ocean is deepest and larger than a lake."],"answer":"The ocean is deeper and larger than a lake.","explanation":"Short adjective + -er + than.","explanation_ar":"الصفة القصيرة + er."},{"q":"How can we fix it? \"taif is more cool than riyadh.\"","options":["taif is cooler than riyadh.","Taif is cooler from Riyadh.","Taif is cooler than Riyadh.","Taif is more cool than Riyadh."],"answer":"Taif is cooler than Riyadh.","explanation":"Short adjective + -er + than.","explanation_ar":"الصفة القصيرة + er."},{"q":"Which is bigger, a lake or an ocean? – ___","options":["An ocean is as big as a lake.","A lake is bigger than an ocean.","An ocean is bigger than a lake.","An ocean is more big than a lake."],"answer":"An ocean is bigger than a lake.","explanation":"Short adjective + -er + than.","explanation_ar":"الصفة القصيرة + er."}],"theme_ar":"عالمنا المدهش","essential_question_ar":"كيف تختلف الأماكن على الأرض بعضها عن بعض؟","can_do":"I can compare places, animals and things with comparative adjectives and as…as.","can_do_ar":"أستطيع أن أقارن الأماكن والحيوانات والأشياء باستخدام صفات المقارنة وas…as."});
